**Q: On a scale of 1 to 10, how hesitant or scared would you be to change your course path, even with the guidance of an automatic simulator?**  
A: It depends on how good the simulator is. If said simulator has been proven sucessful I wouldn't be hesitant but considering the fact that answering the questions based on the subject is not really well. I would say somewhat hesitant because an automatic simulator doesn't have human touch, even if said automatic simulator is giving me recomendations I would still find my academic advisor to deal with deeper of what my situation is. Because there comes a point where you can't automate everything. Everybody passes different courses and fail different courses. Their course plan if they would change in even different way and that requires precision and I dont think a machine could handle, so it still requires human touch. I would be pretty hesistant I would go to someone who knows more like an academic advisor. 

